From 5a55c571833d68b7ddc26d8fd8cb10ee7a558d11 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marc Donovici <azerty10997@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 13:38:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cpu: add IQ4_XS to the repack fast path (reference
 kernels)

IQ4_XS had no entry in ggml_repack_get_optimal_repack_type(), so it never
reached the row-interleaved kernels on any architecture -- despite being the
format most MoE GGUFs ship in. Intel AMX lists IQ4_XS in qtype_has_amx_kernels();
Arm had nothing.

IQ4_XS is IQ4_NL's kvalues_iq4nl codebook carrying K-quant style super-block
scales, so block_iq4_xsx8 mirrors block_q4_Kx8 while keeping iq4_xs's own scale
encoding and its 16-lo/16-hi nibble grouping. The interleaved block is exactly
8 * sizeof(block_iq4_xs), as the repack buffer allocates ggml_nbytes().

This commit adds the layout, repack and portable reference gemv/gemm, registered
only where I8MM exists (the target for the vectorised kernel to follow). Cores
with DOTPROD but no I8MM are deliberately left on the existing path rather than
regressed onto a scalar reference.

Also hardens ggml_backend_cpu_repack_buffer_set_tensor(): init_tensor leaves
extra == nullptr for unclaimed types, and set_tensor dereferenced it without a
check, turning a clear configuration error into a segfault.
